## Dependency policy

This workspace was generated audit-clean and carries the machinery to stay that
way.

```bash
npm run audit:policy          # resolve a lockfile, audit it, fail on anything new
npm run doctor                # diff against the policy shipped by the generator
npx angular-capacitor-workspace doctor --fix   # apply that diff
```

`package.json` holds two policy artefacts:

- **`overrides`** — transitive pins that resolve advisories with no upstream fix.
  Each one exists for a reason recorded in the generator's policy module.
- **`allowScripts`** — the npm ≥ 11.6 install-script allowlist. Everything not
  listed is blocked from running code at install time. CI runs
  `npm ci --strict-allow-scripts`, so a new dependency that wants a postinstall
  fails the build until someone decides it should have one.

Upgrading the generator and running `doctor --fix` is how this workspace picks
up remedies published after it was created.
